{"items":[
{"label":"2A","direction":"supports","claim":"Over three years, the Illumina part of Taiwan NHRI's outsourced sequencing contract fell about 37%, while the PacBio part stayed exactly flat until 2026.","detail":"NHRI (unit 92019239) awards a yearly open-ended contract for outsourced NGS. Group A covers the Illumina platform (items 1–21) and Group B covers PacBio. Group A went to Genomics BioSci & Tech (基龍米克斯) at NT$13,985,910 (Aug 2023), NT$11,213,795 (Sep 2024, −19.8%) and NT$10,341,095 (Sep 2025, −7.8%). The Oct 2026 re-tender budgets Group A at only NT$8,804,000 (−14.9% vs the 2025 award; −37% vs 2023). The 2024 and 2025 awards were follow-on restricted awards (Art. 22(1)(7)) referencing the 2023 contract, so the item list is the same. PacBio stayed at exactly NT$3,989,000 in 2023, 2024 and 2025, so the Illumina-side decline reflects price cuts or reduced scope, not a mechanical carry-over. Caveat: these are contract ceilings, not actual spend.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=92019239&job_number=114B0E0213","date":"2025-09-08","source_name":"Taiwan Government e-Procurement System (via pcc-api.openfun.app)","source_type":"procurement","quote":"A組Illumina定序平台","strength":"strong","why_new":"Known items cover NHRI's per-genome WGS rate and the end of its 6000 tenders; this multi-year time series of outsourced Illumina contract values is new."},
{"label":"2A","direction":"supports","claim":"NHRI's total outsourced NGS ceiling fell about 68% from 2021 to 2026, and its own NovaSeq 6000 service and kit buying stopped at the same time, so this research account's Illumina-linked spend shrank sharply.","detail":"Outsourced NGS awards were NT$31.39M (Apr 2021, single vendor Taiwan Genome Alliance), NT$17.97M (2023), NT$15.20M (2024) and NT$14.33M (2025). The 2026 budget is NT$9.9975M (Illumina 8.804M + PacBio 1.1935M). The budget held at NT$24.87M in 2023–25 while awards fell. In-house, the four-unit NovaSeq 6000 service contract cost NT$13.8M for Dec 2023–Dec 2024 and has no successor in PCC title searches. Derived: Illumina-linked spend was at least ~NT$27.8M a year in 2023–24 (13.8M service + 13.99M outsourced Illumina, before kits) vs ~NT$8.8–10.3M in 2025–26, roughly −63% to −68%.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=92019239&job_number=115B0D0286","date":"2026-10-01","source_name":"Taiwan Government e-Procurement System","source_type":"procurement","quote":"委外檢測開口契約: 次世代基因體核酸定序實驗","strength":"medium","why_new":"Quantifies the combined fall in in-house plus outsourced spend at NHRI; F718 only noted that NHRI moved to outsourcing."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"against","claim":"NHRI paid a flat NT$3.45M per unit per year (about US$110K) for NovaSeq 6000 service from 2020 to 2023, so service pricing did not erode before the fleet left contract.","detail":"Four-unit, one-year 6000 maintenance was NT$14.0M (Dec 2020; budget 14.8M, single bidder Genetech/均泰, Art. 22(1)(4)) and NT$13.8M (Dec 2023, single bidder, Art. 22(1)(7)), a −1.4% change over three years. Derived: NT$3.45M per unit ≈ US$107–110K at ~31.5 NT$/US$. That is ~38% below the US Silver list of $175,653, but the price is stable. No 6000 service award appears after the Dec 2023–Dec 2024 term.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=92019239&job_number=112B0D0681","date":"2023-12-12","source_name":"Taiwan Government e-Procurement System","source_type":"procurement","quote":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000定序系統4台維護1年","strength":"medium","why_new":"Per-unit 6000 service price and its 2020–23 path in Taiwan are not in the ledger (F624/F517 cover US/Canadian federal plans only)."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"against","claim":"Taiwan's flagship hospital (NTUH) signed new three-year reagent contracts for retired or legacy Illumina platforms that run to 2028–2029.","detail":"NTUH awarded MiniSeq mid-output 300-cycle kits (7 items) for Jun 2025–May 2028 at NT$2,148,230, sole-source under Art. 22(1)(4), with one bidder (Genetech). That runs well past MiniSeq end of sale (30 Sep 2025). It also awarded NextSeq 500/550-class mid-output v2.5 300-cycle kits for Aug 2026–Jul 2029 at NT$4,410,000 (restricted tender, Art. 22(1)(2), single bidder, 2.2% below the NT$4,508,000 floor). Clinical labs keep legacy Illumina boxes on reagent contracts for 3+ years, which fits a slow, sticky high-price tail and is consistent with management's 'stays for years' framing.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=3.9.20.1&job_number=TD150300","date":"2026-06-10","source_name":"Taiwan Government e-Procurement System","source_type":"procurement","quote":"中通量300鹼基循環定序試劑組v2.5開口合約","strength":"medium","why_new":"These are new dated legacy-platform reagent commitments to 2028–29 at an Asian clinical flagship; earlier tail items are US, Canadian, UK and EU service contracts."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"against","claim":"Kaohsiung VGH bought outsourced clinical WGS at NT$12,800 per genome in Dec 2025 and Jan 2026, and a bidder linked to AXELIOS (Centogene) bid higher, not lower.","detail":"Kaohsiung VGH bought 210 oral-cancer genomes for NT$2,688,000 (Dec 2025, one bidder; the original bid of NT$13,500 per genome was cut to the floor). It bought 250 women's-medicine genomes including blood extraction for NT$3,200,000 (Jan 2026). Both prices derive to NT$12,800 per genome (~US$400), awarded to Genomics BioSci. In the Jan 2026 lot, Centogene APAC (權拓基因) bid NT$3,498,750 (NT$13,995 per genome, +9%) and was ruled non-compliant on documents. This extends the flat NT$12,800 rate to a fourth hospital and into 2026.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=3.32.82&job_number=ST1412017","date":"2026-01-30","source_name":"Taiwan Government e-Procurement System","source_type":"procurement","quote":"權拓基因股份有限公司","strength":"medium","why_new":"D073 and F744 cover three earlier awards. Kaohsiung VGH's 2026 awards and the Centogene APAC bid are new."},
{"label":"2A","direction":"against","claim":"Taipei Medical University's Sep 2026 research WGS award implies NT$9,800 per genome, the same rate NHRI paid in Oct 2024, so research WGS pricing has been flat for two years.","detail":"TMU115-029 was awarded at NT$3,057,600 (= floor) to Taiwan Genome Alliance (台基盟), the single bidder; the original bid was NT$3,346,512. The Ministry of Education subsidy was NT$3,369,600. Derived: 3,057,600 / 9,800 = exactly 312 genomes, and 3,369,600 / 312 = NT$10,800 subsidy per genome. The genome count is inferred, not stated. The tender required ≥2 Illumina high-throughput sequencers plus a PacBio Sequel IIe. The research rate stays ~23% below the hospital rate of NT$12,800.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=03724606&job_number=TMU115-029","date":"2026-09-29","source_name":"Taiwan Government e-Procurement System","source_type":"procurement","quote":"具二台以上Illumina高通量次世代定序儀","strength":"medium","why_new":"F761 covered only the tender's Illumina qualification; the award value and implied flat NT$9,800 research price are new."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"On NTUH's NT$297M flagship WGS reagent-with-instrument contract, the hospital pushed the sole bidder down 10.8%, from NT$332.9M to the floor.","detail":"K114031 runs 1 Mar 2026–28 Feb 2029 and bundles WGS reagents with instruments (a reagent-rental structure). Genetech (均泰, Illumina's distributor) was the only bidder. Its original bid of NT$332,927,500 was awarded at NT$296,999,880, NT$120 under the NT$297,000,000 floor. The first round failed with no bidders. Even without competition, the large clinical buyer used its budget-floor mechanism to extract ~11% off the vendor's ask, about US$1.1M a year.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=3.9.20.1&job_number=K114031","date":"2026-02-05","source_name":"Taiwan Government e-Procurement System","source_type":"procurement","quote":"次世代全基因體定序試劑3項(附儀器)開口合約","strength":"medium","why_new":"F715 gave only the contract value; the bid-to-award concession and the reagent-with-instrument bundling are new."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"Two Taiwanese veterans' hospitals pay very different prices for the same Illumina NextSeq 2000 P3 kit: Taipei VGH about 49% more than Taichung VGH.","detail":"Taipei VGH (1150157V, May 2026, single bidder Genetech) paid NT$235,000 per P3 set (15 sets, NT$3,525,000) and NT$201,000 per P4 XLEAP set (18 sets). Taichung VGH (115A018, Sep 2026, single bidder Genomics BioSci) paid NT$9,480,000 for 60 P3 kits ≈ NT$158,000 each and NT$2,640,000 for 12 P4 kits ≈ NT$220,000 each (derived from the tender quantities). The P3 gap is +49% at Taipei, while P4 is 9% cheaper there. Prices depend on the channel and the deal, not a list. That fits individualized, negotiable pricing rather than a uniform price floor.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=3.32.80&job_number=1150157V","date":"2026-05-12","source_name":"Taiwan Government e-Procurement System","source_type":"procurement","quote":"P3 大通量定序試劑組","strength":"weak","why_new":"F713, F717 and D071 cover each hospital separately. The cross-hospital comparison of the same kit and the two competing Illumina channels are new."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"against","claim":"Taipei VGH's mid-throughput Illumina reagent commitments rose roughly 60–70% between its 2023–25 and 2025–28 contracts.","detail":"Dec 2023 (1120652Y) bought a 2-year 'high-throughput reagent set' of 29 sets for NT$6.67M (~NT$230K per set). The new cycle stacks three awards: 1140732E (Nov 2025, 2-year lot NT$3.942M, ≈17 sets at ~NT$230K) plus 1150157V (May 2026: 15 P3 + 18 P4 sets, NT$7.143M). That is ~NT$11.1M and ~50 sets vs NT$6.67M and 29 sets (derived; the Apr 2025 P4 contract 1140134V may overlap). Clinical mid-throughput usage at this hospital is growing, not stalling.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=3.32.80&job_number=1140732E","date":"2025-11-25","source_name":"Taiwan Government e-Procurement System","source_type":"procurement","quote":"高通量定序試劑組等7項2年單價開口契約","strength":"weak","why_new":"Known items give only per-set prices at Taipei VGH; the contract-cycle volume comparison is new."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"Taiwan's public procurement shows no NovaSeq 6000 kit buying since Dec 2023 and no NovaSeq X kit line by name, because high-throughput work moved into bundled or outsourced contracts.","detail":"Title searches on PCC for 'NovaSeq' return 19 records, all at NHRI, ending with 16 S4 v1.5 kits and 6000 service in Dec 2023. Searches for 'S4' found only those NHRI rows, and '25B' found no sequencing rows. In 2024–26, hospital high-throughput sequencing appears only as reagents-with-instrument lots (NTUH NT$32.5M and NT$297M) or as per-genome outsourcing to Genomics BioSci and Taiwan Genome Alliance. So the share of 6000 kit value is 100% through 2023 and there are no observable kit lines in 2024–26. The requested 6000-vs-X kit-line count cannot be built from Taiwan's public data.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/searchbytitle?query=NovaSeq&page=1","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"Taiwan Government e-Procurement System (title search)","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"This is a method finding: it records that the Taiwan kit-line vein is dry, so later agents need not repeat it."},
{"label":"2B","direction":"supports","claim":"A Taiwanese clinical center and NHRI are adding long-read capacity next to Illumina in 2026.","detail":"Taipei VGH awarded a 3-year 'third-generation sequencing whole-genome reagents (6 items, with equipment)' contract (M11476V, Mar 2026) at NT$11.3M to Genomics BioSci, origin USA (likely PacBio); one bidder after two failed rounds. NHRI opened a vendor-quote solicitation on 12 Oct 2026 for a long-read sequencing system for its new F building. Meanwhile, NHRI's own outsourced PacBio budget for 2026 fell to NT$1.19M from NT$3.99M. The net effect for Illumina is mixed; this is a weak signal.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=3.32.80&job_number=M11476V","date":"2026-03-11","source_name":"Taiwan Government e-Procurement System","source_type":"procurement","quote":"三代定序全基因體基因檢測試劑6項(含設備)","strength":"weak","why_new":"Taiwan long-read adoption was not in the ledger (Taiwan CDC nanopore items F749 and F750 cover ONT only)."}
